### Legacy API retained in new implementation

<details><summary>Expand</summary>

Note that the internals of the `k_work` and `k_work_q` structures have changed completely, and it is more clearly stated that code is not permitted to examine their contents through anything other than documented public API.

```
typedef void (*k_work_handler_t)(struct k_work *work);

struct k_work;
K_WORK_DEFINE(work, work_handler);
void k_work_init(struct k_work *work,
                 k_work_handler_t handler);
void k_work_submit_to_queue(struct k_work_q *work_q,
                            struct k_work *work)
void k_work_submit(struct k_work *work);

struct k_work_poll;
void k_work_poll_init(struct k_work_poll *work,
                      k_work_handler_t handler);
int k_work_poll_submit_to_queue(struct k_work_q *work_q,
                                struct k_work_poll *work,
                                struct k_poll_event *events,
                                int num_events,
                                k_timeout_t timeout)
int k_work_poll_submit(struct k_work_poll *work,
                       struct k_poll_event *events,
                       int num_events,
                       k_timeout_t timeout)
int k_work_poll_cancel(struct k_work_poll *work);

struct k_work_q;
```
</details>

### Legacy API that is to be deprecated that has inline replacements.

<details><summary>Expand</summary>

Notes:
* Scheduling delayable work cannot fail in the new implementation, so error returns for delayed submit functions will not be observed.
* Canceling delayable work cannot fail, but does indicate when the work is still in progress.  A best effort is made to infer a return value consistent with old cancel behavior

