### API that is implemented pending evidence of need

<details><summary>Expand</summary>

In the old implementation the remaining time before submission of a delayed item was often used in an attempt to determine whether the submission or execution had occurred.  With the new API supporting both schedule and reschedule semantics this may not be necessary.  (The Linux delayable work API does not support reading remaining time.)

If updating to the new API provides evidence that inspecting remaining time has a useful purpose this API will be documented and made permanent.  If not, it will be removed.

```
k_ticks_t k_work_delayable_expires_get(const struct k_work_delayable *dwork);
k_ticks_t k_work_delayable_remaining_get(const struct k_work_delayable *dwork);
```
</details>

