Cleaned up some documentation, and updated commit 6f827a1f6cc4b0362d0627b2a16c442918616fca which works around a tcp2 API misuse, to more clearly document what's going on and the solution alternatives.

@jukkar I had planned to address the TODO this adds in subsys/net/ip/tcp2.c by refactoring to use the new API directly instead of the legacy one.  However, while looking into that I found that the TCP2 implementation uses work handlers that can block, in particular `tcp_send_process`.

Blocking in the system workqueue is not a great idea.  It may be appropriate for the TCP2 to create its own work queue, just as the USB infrastructure does (to deconflict with the Bluetooth infrastructure).
